       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Dose:** Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. The usual maximum for adults is 3,200 mg/day under medical supervision. The OTC limit is 1,200 mg/day.\n- **Single dose:** 1,600 mg is twice the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.\n- **Risks:** At this dose the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events rises sharply. Higher doses don't give more analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg by mouth, four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum for this patient\n- **400\u2013600 mg by mouth, every 6 hours** for typical analgesia\n- **1,600 mg/day total**, for example 400 mg four times daily\n\nIf you do want 1,600 mg four times daily, tell me and add a note on the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with that documented, though pharmacy will likely flag it. Otherwise, tell me which dose to enter."
      }
